cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Inverse in research or teaching, please cite this software and record the commit hash you used."
type: software
title: "Inverse: An interactive notebook for inverse problems"
authors:
  - family-names: "Mujahid"
    given-names: "Burhan"
    email: "burhanmujahid552@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/burhan-mujahid/inverse-notebook"
url: "https://github.com/burhan-mujahid/inverse-notebook"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A browser-based computational notebook for working backward from a desired
  result. A cantilever beam prototype demonstrates constrained inverse solving
  with exact locks, weighted relative changes, reachable output intervals,
  and reversible proposals. Its small JavaScript engine supports positive
  monomial relationships with log-linear constraints.
keywords:
  - inverse problems
  - interactive computation
  - convex optimization
  - constraint solving
  - human-computer interaction
  - explorable explanations
  - scientific computing
